{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And Aaron saw</b> — The sense of this verse is that he saw them disposed toward evil (Exodus 32:22), drawn toward the calf, so he arose and built an altar and proclaimed, \"A feast to YHWH tomorrow,\" so that they would sacrifice to the unique Name upon the altar that he built for His name, and they would not build altars for shame, and their intention in the sacrifices would be for YHWH alone. And it is possible that he said \"tomorrow\" in order to stall them — perhaps Moses would come and they would abandon the calf. But they rose early in the morning and offered burnt offerings and brought peace offerings, and Scripture does not say \"they offered to it burnt offerings and brought to it peace offerings\" — the reason being that among them were some whose intention was toward the Name of the Holy One, blessed be He, as Aaron had said, while others were corrupters who sacrificed to the calf. And concerning these the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Moses (Exodus 32:8), \"They bowed down to it and sacrificed to it,\" for they were the sinners. And had Aaron himself been the one offering the sacrifices, Scripture would have stated simply \"and he offered burnt offerings and brought peace offerings,\" for his intention was toward the name of YHWH, whereas their minds were set on the calf that they had made, and the owners were rendering it piggul."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:19:26.437018182Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}